WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:02.949
This video is sponsored by Brilliant.

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:07.750
Start learning for free with the link in the
description and the first 200 get 20% off

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.980
the annual premium subscription.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:17.120
Zhang Yiming was born April 1982 in China’s
Fujian province.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.539
His mother, a nurse, and father the owner
of an electronics factory, were unusual in

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:27.810
that they gave their son the freedom to explore
his interests - namely, technology.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:33.870
This, little did they know, would put Zhang
on the path to become China’s Mark Zuckerberg.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:39.490
In 2001, he left to study engineering near
Beijing, which he chose for the “pretty

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.290
girls and winter snow”.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:46.900
While Zuckerberg, two years younger and six
thousand miles away, entered Harvard, met

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:54.290
his wife, and started Facebook, Zhang fixed
computers, met his wife, and built his startup.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:59.559
After several failed ventures, in 2012 he
founded a new company called ByteDance from

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.129
his small Beijing apartment.

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:08.530
And although his path was rockier than Zuckerberg’s,
it was no less abrupt or explosive.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:13.140
By the end of its first year, Facebook had
registered one million users.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:18.810
ByteDance’s first breakthrough - a Chinese
video-sharing app - had 100 million.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:24.889
Then, having conquered the Chinese market,
the company turned global, buying its competitor

00:01:24.889 --> 00:01:32.049
and the spiritual successor to Vine, called
Musical.ly in 2017 - later rebranded as ‘TikTok’

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:33.749
outside of China.

00:01:33.749 --> 00:01:39.659
The app - now ubiquitous among young people
everywhere - makes it almost too easy to shoot,

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:45.729
edit, and share videos, usually in the form
of dancing, comedy skits, and stream-of-consciousness

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:47.409
monologues.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:52.950
The real genius of TikTok, however, and what
sets it apart from Snapchat, Instagram, and

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:58.219
Facebook, is the part you don’t see - the
much-alluded-to, guarded-like-a-state-secret

00:01:58.219 --> 00:01:59.549
algorithm.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:06.770
Rather than by following friends, TikTok learns,
on its own, exactly what you like as you mindlessly

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.860
scroll through its endless feed of videos.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:14.890
You don’t need to follow, like, or search
for it to understand your preferences.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.100
And the more you scroll, the better it gets
at reading your mind.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:25.380
This is also what makes it so addicting - unlike
Twitter or Instagram where you can stay up-to-date

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:31.820
on your timeline, TikTok will keep you entertained
for however many hours you allow it.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:37.550
Knowing this, its 2 billion downloads in its
only four years of existence and ByteDance’s

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:44.130
position as the most valuable private company
in the world are impressive but not altogether

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.650
surprising.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:51.720
Equally so Zhang’s personal wealth of around
$16 billion - making him the tenth richest

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.870
person in China and 61st in the world.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:03:01.420
Today, at 38 years old, he’s still described
as the nerdy, awkward, uncharismatic, but

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.540
undeniably resourceful mirror-image of Zuckerberg.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:10.120
In his rare public appearances, he often comes
across as robotic and overly-rational.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:17.330
There is, however, one obvious major difference
between these two internet titans: Zhang built

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.850
his company in China.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:23.850
While Facebook had to first allow a foreign
government to interfere in a presidential

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:29.490
election before Congress would even begin
considering regulation, TikTok faced legal

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.830
constraints from the very beginning.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:37.240
What’s remarkable about its success is that
it’s neither a clone of a foreign-made app,

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:41.670
nor, like Huawei, aided financially by the
Chinese government.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:47.480
Just as impressive, it resisted acquisition
by Alibaba, Tencent, or any other deep-pocketed

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.610
tech giant.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:55.900
By not doing so, TikTok arguably became China’s
first true consumer technology export success

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:02.709
story - and all on its own - overcoming its
limitations despite being based in China,

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.660
not because of it.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:09.720
Prevailing in this challenging environment
affords Zhang even greater praise, but also

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:15.980
subjects his empire to a potential collapse
just as instantaneous as it was built.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:21.639
It took only a few short years for TikTok
to surpass, in downloads, some of the biggest

00:04:21.639 --> 00:04:23.930
companies in the world.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:31.479
But it may take only a few emphatic pen strokes
for all that progress to be lost.

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:38.099
On June 29th, 2020, the second-most populous
country in the world and by far TikTok’s

00:04:38.099 --> 00:04:44.680
biggest market, the Republic of India, banned
it, along with 60 other Chinese mobile apps

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.970
accused of stealing and sending user data
outside of the country.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:54.660
Ironically, this came as a surprise to a nation
whose Great Firewall has methodically banned,

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:58.349
censored, and regulated foreign media for
decades.

00:04:58.349 --> 00:05:04.120
With this one swift move, millions of viewers
and creators, some of whom depended on the

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:08.999
app for a significant portion of their living,
were simply out of luck.

00:05:08.999 --> 00:05:13.830
Just as significant, was the potential domino
effect this decision could have.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:19.669
TikTok’s largest source of downloads this
year, in order, are India, Brazil, and the

00:05:19.669 --> 00:05:25.099
U.S. - the latter of which is a prime contender
for the next domino to fall.

00:05:25.099 --> 00:05:30.059
This, in fact, undersells the significance
of the U.S. market.

00:05:30.059 --> 00:05:35.860
When divided by platform, it’s revealed
as a major source of iPhone users - who spend,

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:39.330
on average, two and a half times more on apps.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:45.120
What this means is that while Americans account
for only 10% of TikTok’s overall user base,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.289
they make up an incredible 56% of its revenue.

00:05:49.289 --> 00:05:55.509
A ban by the U.S. would not simply limit its
growth but require a fundamental restructuring

00:05:55.509 --> 00:06:01.240
of its business - to say nothing of the potential
for other countries to follow its lead.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:04.830
What, then, is the likelihood of such a ban?

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:08.039
And would it be justified?

00:06:08.039 --> 00:06:13.400
Even before any real arguments are made, fear
of TikTok may, to some, seem reasonable if

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:18.710
only because such fear is so widespread, and
came about so suddenly.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:24.050
The list of skeptics, even prior to India’s
ban, is long.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:28.960
After a regional office was established in
Sydney, Australian authorities began investigating

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:34.169
the app on suspicion of foreign interference
and violations of data privacy.

00:06:34.169 --> 00:06:39.749
Both the U.S. Democratic and Republican national
committees have asked staffers not to install

00:06:39.749 --> 00:06:44.990
the app or to buy a second phone when using
it for campaign work.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:49.059
As have the U.S. Department of State, Homeland
Security, and military.

00:06:49.059 --> 00:06:54.630
Even private companies have followed suit
- including the bank Wells Fargo and Amazon,

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:58.400
although the latter retracted its statement
shortly afterward.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:02.939
Tensions reached a new high when the Trump
administration strongly alluded to a ban at

00:07:02.939 --> 00:07:08.529
the same time as the president’s re-election
campaign bought Facebook ads saying “TikTok

00:07:08.529 --> 00:07:13.080
is spying on you” and have been “caught
red-handed”.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.839
Should this decision be made, several levers
are at its disposal.

00:07:16.839 --> 00:07:21.669
First, The Committee on Foreign Investment,
whose job is to monitor national security

00:07:21.669 --> 00:07:27.020
concerns, could force ByteDance to sell-off
its American operations to an approved buyer.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:31.869
Alternatively, the Trump administration could
invoke the International Emergency Economic

00:07:31.869 --> 00:07:37.210
Powers Act, or place TikTok on the Entity
List, which would force its removal from the

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.919
app stores.

00:07:38.919 --> 00:07:44.469
As in the case of Huawei’s ban almost exactly
one year ago, skeptics are quick to point

00:07:44.469 --> 00:07:48.869
out the preferential treatment it would give
to American competitors.

00:07:48.869 --> 00:07:54.649
As if on cue, Instagram is expected to launch
its TikTok competitor, called Reels, in the

00:07:54.649 --> 00:07:56.149
U.S. this August.

00:07:56.149 --> 00:08:02.490
Snapchat, Byte, Likee, and YouTube have also
tried replicating the concept.

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:07.749
Even Netflix listed the app as a competitor
in its latest letter to shareholders - a sign

00:08:07.749 --> 00:08:11.529
of just how time-consuming it’s become.

00:08:11.529 --> 00:08:16.780
Also like Huawei, the claims made against
it are sometimes vague, hard to disprove,

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.949
and yet also extremely consequential.

00:08:19.949 --> 00:08:24.520
Several independent observers allege the app
censors content in accordance with Mainland

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.559
Chinese guidelines.

00:08:26.559 --> 00:08:32.300
For example, in the absence of videos covering
the pro-democracy protests in Hong Kong.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:37.270
The company has publicly admitted to limiting
the reach of disabled, queer, and overweight

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:41.900
creators, which it claims was for their own
protection against bullying, before changing

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.070
policies.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:47.940
A ‘bug’, it says, was responsible for
showing no views on videos related to Black

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.740
Lives Matter.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:54.850
On one hand, the nebulousness of the algorithm
allows anyone to claim censorship without

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:57.100
strong supporting evidence.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:01.460
On the other, this provides cover for TikTok
in that it can always remind them that the

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:06.581
algorithm is based on their preferences and
that any perceived manipulation is only a

00:09:06.581 --> 00:09:09.080
reflection of their behavior.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:16.010
More concretely, the company has paid $5 million
and $150,000, respectively, to U.S. and Korean

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:21.410
authorities for collecting the personal information
of children without parental consent.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:27.710
However, unlike Huawei, the controversy surrounds
not critical communications infrastructure

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:31.090
but a lip-syncing, dancing app for teens.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:36.480
A TikTok ban raises far more eyebrows because
the idea of such an app presenting a threat

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:40.500
to national security is a much less intuitive
argument.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:46.530
This, critics would say, is precisely what
makes it such an effective tool - nobody suspects

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:47.530
it.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:52.830
A preview of what it could become if left
unregulated is the version of the app in China,

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:57.910
which is home to a much older audience, is
used by police to spread information, and

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.650
has advanced face recognition.

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:06.030
Such was the backdrop of skepticism against
which more recent discoveries were made.

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:11.240
When the beta of the next version of iOS was
released this summer, a new privacy feature

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:15.130
was included which alerts users when an app
copies their clipboard.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:21.120
It didn’t take long before videos like this
one emerged, showing TikTok almost constantly

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.680
reading whatever is copied.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:29.010
More careful digging also found the app recording
a users’ screen size, as well as other information

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.130
about their device.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.490
These findings are a trap.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:39.790
Well-intentioned as they may be, they only
distract from other, far more serious concerns.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:45.190
Experts agree that TikTok’s data collection
practices are not only not rare, but actually

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:50.380
quite restrained when compared with other
ad-based services like Facebook.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:55.280
Reddit and LinkedIn, for instance, were also
caught reading the clipboard, which they say

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:57.420
is used to prevent spam.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:02.410
ByteDance has explicitly repeated that it
does not employ moderators in China and that

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:07.120
U.S. data is stored in the U.S., with backups
in Singapore.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:13.160
By narrowly focusing on the technical details,
the issue is reframed as one of privacy, which

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:19.800
could just as easily be applied to any application,
including and especially those based in America.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:25.570
It’s no coincidence, rather, that those
most familiar with Chinese politics are also

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:28.030
the app’s most vocal critics.

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:34.250
TikTok is not just another social network
because China is not just another country.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:38.900
This is also not to say that the company doesn’t
mean what it says.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:43.890
One of the most unfortunate byproducts of
its place of birth is that TikTok may be dangerous

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:46.320
through no fault of its own.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:51.920
China’s 2017 National Intelligence Law compels
all companies with information stored within

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:58.360
its borders to hand-over data at its request
- without the constraints of courts or warrants.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:04.180
If this sounds only theoretical, ByteDance’s
first app was shut down in 2018 by the National

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:09.170
Radio and Television Administration, after
which Zhang apologized for his poor adherence

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:11.780
to socialist core values.

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:15.890
In practice, this control extends much further
than its borders.

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:21.920
A company need not be based or even physically
present, at all, in China for it to be beholden

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.160
financially.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:28.850
It does not matter that ByteDance is incorporated
in the Cayman Islands, or that Zoom is headquartered

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:35.640
in California - or that the NBA is, in every
sense of the word, American - for their checks

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:38.060
are signed elsewhere.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:40.520
None of this is particularly new.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:44.880
China has effectively operated a separate
internet for years, which foreign companies

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:48.140
have gained access to by self-censoring.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:53.830
What has changed is that, until recently this
has been relatively easy to deny or ignore.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:59.420
Now, at a time of record bipartisanship in
favor of a tougher response to China, it is

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.640
no longer possible to feign ignorance.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:08.040
Whereas before appeasing China was the common-sense
profit-maximizing business tactic to gain

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:14.840
access to its 1.4 billion users with minimal
casualties elsewhere, now there’s a tradeoff.

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:19.940
And as companies are forced to confront this
reality, they will inevitably decide on one

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.680
of three general approaches:

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:26.210
The first group will rip-off the bandaid as
quickly as possible.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:31.350
They’ll cut their losses by leaving the
Chinese market entirely and spending massively

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:36.910
on PR against their competitors who don’t,
while facing backlash from investors.

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.950
A second group will do just the opposite.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:45.050
These, mostly Chinese-based companies will
see international expansion as more liability

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:48.730
than its worth and leave the non-Chinese market.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:52.960
Notably, this does not constrain them to the
mainland, but would likely include developing

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:56.950
markets which can’t afford to be scrupulous
when offered investment.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:14:02.340
Finally, some especially international companies
will see either option as too high a cost

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:08.980
to bear and make the highest-reward, yet highest-risk
gamble - to juggle both.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:13.840
These firms will split in two, and each division
will try its hardest to distance itself from

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.010
the other.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:20.570
If they fail, pressure will grow until enough
value is lost that a deal will be made - and

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:24.900
one or both divisions will be sold to a disinterested
investor.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:28.800
TikTok is a prime example of the third strategy.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:35.060
In the last several months alone, it has hired
a new American, ex-Disney CEO, announced its

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:41.360
plans to add another 10,000 U.S. jobs in the
next three years, doubled its lobbying budget,

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:47.240
and, after the National Security Law was promulgated
in Hong Kong, left the Special Administrative

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.930
Region entirely.

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:54.560
However, with an election less than 100 days
away, it seems unlikely these moves will be

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:56.780
nearly drastic enough.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:15:01.780
Even a majority sale to a U.S. investor may
not assuage fears during a time of intense

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:05.980
scrutiny towards China and a presidency at
stake.

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:11.020
Such is the predicament: it’s impossible
to divorce any action from these political

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.020
circumstances.

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:17.660
And yet, that doesn’t automatically disqualify
arguments in favor of a ban.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:22.160
It is rare but not the least bit contradictory
to admit that:

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:26.990
It is politically popular to attack companies
for their ties to the PRC, and would still

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:31.070
be whether or not such fears were founded;
AND

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:36.420
TikTok poses a very real potential threat
to the interests of the U.S. and other countries,

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:42.640
simply because of its ties to China; AND
There is a deeply troubling, growing tendency

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:47.400
to associate anything broadly labeled ‘Chinese’
as untrustworthy.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:53.060
To ban TikTok would create a kind of Great
American Firewall - against the will of American

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:57.779
users, and yet, not doing so would subject
the country to greater risk.

00:15:57.779 --> 00:16:04.690
There is, however, one neutral path forward:
To pass regulation governing where data can

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:10.770
be stored, requiring disclosure of the algorithm,
local ownership, and creating mechanisms for

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:13.000
auditing and enforcement.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:17.390
Doing so, although seen as less politically
‘strong’, would subject all companies

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:21.350
- foreign and otherwise - to the same fair
standards.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:27.550
TikTok would remain, giving American companies
greater competition and incentive to innovate,

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:32.080
companies like Facebook would be forced to
respect their users’ privacy, and all without

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:36.010
provoking backlash for targeting a specific
group of people.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:40.790
This is a long-term solution for a long-term
problem.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:46.360
Because although TikTok was one of the first
Chinese apps to go global, it certainly won’t

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.200
be the last.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:54.140
There will be another Huawei, another Zoom,
and another TikTok, and how the world responds

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:57.590
now will set the tone of what’s to come.

00:16:57.590 --> 00:17:03.510
TikTok is the product of one man’s intense
interest in technology and curiosity to learn

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:04.510
more.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:09.569
Its rise proves that the next big idea won’t
necessarily come from Facebook, Google, or

00:17:09.569 --> 00:17:12.520
Apple - it could come from you.

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:16.370
If you’re watching this video, you’re
clearly interested in tech and motivated to

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:17.440
learn on your own.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:22.730
And you can take the next step on your entrepreneurial
journey with the programming, cryptocurrency,

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:25.750
and machine learning courses on Brilliant.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:30.880
At a time when school is closed and classes
are going online, now is the time to take

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:36.350
charge of your own education and Brilliant
is just the place to do so - with its beautifully-made,

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:41.940
interactive, step-by-step lessons available
on both its mobile app and website.

